\n\n$$\n100%+7.5%=107.5%=1.075\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.075:$\n\n$$\n32\\times 1.075=34.4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total cost after tax is $$34.40.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f90ea994-79f2-5409-bf96-306803b4ef01" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Percentage Increase: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dbbbdc0-5f26-50ac-832c-26ac54a8ebaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$28.25$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455040} {:answer/id #uuid "7aef5edd-bcf2-522a-8aad-62129774a06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$28.89$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455129} {:answer/id #uuid "806ad696-2e72-5098-a173-5dd7c7fe403e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$29.00$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455135} {:answer/id #uuid "9fb9c83d-5e90-5a24-8df2-5719d471084d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$29.50$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455189} {:answer/id #uuid "c1cae2f4-8869-502e-8347-ca0f1f88e5f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$27.99$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aef5edd-bcf2-522a-8aad-62129774a06a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$28.89$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455129} :answer-field/id #uuid "96faa079-59bb-54c0-a73c-46a0849034fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93d6474a-bde5-548e-95ba-be3229625fd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-326519" :question/problem "A lunch combo costs $$27$ before tax. If a $7%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total price after tax?" :question/worked-solution "To find the total price after tax, we apply a $7%$ increase to the original cost.\n\nIncreasing by $7%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+7%=107%=1.07\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.07:$\n\n$$\n27\\times 1.07=28.89.\n$$\n\nSo, the total price after tax is $$28.89.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f90ea994-79f2-5409-bf96-306803b4ef01" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Percentage Increase: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3774f39e-cf33-5cc6-8237-87d85e3b040a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3774f39e-cf33-5cc6-8237-87d85e3b040a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454991} :answer-field/id #uuid "68102a27-22cb-5f24-873f-402739528011" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46812e7d-8475-5386-b10a-611a622fce90" :question/math-academy-id "q-326531" :question/problem "Last year, a library had $8,000$ visitors. This year, the number of visitors is $25%$ greater than last year. How many visitors did the library have this year?\n\nThe library had\n{{field-1}}\nvisitors this year." :question/worked-solution "To find the number of visitors this year, we apply a $25%$ increase to the previous year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $25%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+25%=125%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n125%=\\frac{125}{100}=1.25\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original number of visitors by $1.25:$\n\n$$\n8,000\\times 1.25=10,000\n$$\n\nSo, the library had $10,000$ visitors this year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152297 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "88d0f4ad-a3f9-5275-b5d5-a9973bf63ebf" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Percentage Increases Greater Than 100%"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91b6186e-23d5-5663-b44e-27caaf7401cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91b6186e-23d5-5663-b44e-27caaf7401cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455168} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b69a06-07c4-5dd9-b035-c36177bbc75c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9940990b-7568-5339-8565-7a872a78726e" :question/math-academy-id "q-327647" :question/problem "A number $x$ is $400%$ greater than $120.$ Find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$  \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find a number $400%$ *greater than* $120,$ we apply a new percentage of  \n\n$$\n100%+400%=500%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting our percentage to a decimal:  \n\n$$\n500%=\\frac{500}{100}=5\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $400%$ greater than $120,$ we multiply $120$ by $5:$  \n\n$$\n5\\cdot 120=600\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=600.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152298 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbb0103d-d686-575a-8ef8-81640227f4dc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Word Problems Involving Percentage Increases Greater Than 100%"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "696ac1e8-7b4c-5b8f-a087-5edde831081b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "696ac1e8-7b4c-5b8f-a087-5edde831081b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455096} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf4af0e1-0991-503c-a6cc-dd355c3175c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "102c884a-37a0-5477-a486-ce757122c1eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-327649" :question/problem "Last year, a factory produced $800$ bicycles. This year, production is $150%$ greater than last year. How many bicycles did the factory produce this year?\n\nThe factory produced\n{{field-1}}\nbicycles this year." :question/worked-solution "To find this year's bicycle production, we apply a $150%$ increase to last year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $150%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+150%=250%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n250%=\\frac{250}{100}=2.5\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $2.5:$\n\n$$\n800\\times 2.5=2,000\n$$\n\nSo, the factory produced $2000$ bicycles this year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152298 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbb0103d-d686-575a-8ef8-81640227f4dc" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Word Problems Involving Percentage Increases Greater Than 100%"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df007cf1-918d-5b8c-8b5a-9369b1e74f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df007cf1-918d-5b8c-8b5a-9369b1e74f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455288} :answer-field/id #uuid "456f04b0-7b52-594e-ac43-23369cc54177" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f47719f0-1c2b-56f4-84a7-999378811070" :question/math-academy-id "q-354520" :question/problem "An artist painted $60$ portraits last year. This year, her output is $400%$ greater than last year. How many portraits did the artist paint this year?\n\nThe artist painted\n{{field-1}}\nportraits this year." :question/worked-solution "To find this year's portrait output, we apply a $400%$ increase to last year's figure.\n\nIncreasing by $400%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+400%=500%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n500%=\\frac{500}{100}=5\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original amount by $5:$\n\n$$\n60\\times 5=300\n$$\n\nSo, the artist painted $300$ portraits this year."}]}
